From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nowon <nowon@noreply.pepecoin.surf>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:02:55 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 093/144] GreatDANE: harden sign_dane_macos.py (NGD round 2:
 M1, M2, L2, L3, L5, L7)

- M1: inside a mapped bundle, only the main executable named by that bundle's own CFBundleExecutable
  (.app Contents/Info.plist; .framework [Versions/*/]Resources/Info.plist) is signed with the bundle.
  Every other Mach-O or nested bundle is refused until it gets its own row. sign-map.tsv header now
  says this, which corrects the old "every Mach-O must match a row" claim.
- M2: the path guard works on the realpath, case-insensitively, with the /System/Volumes/Data alias
  folded. It always refuses /Volumes/Dane and its " N"/"-N" variants, any component containing
  "danenotarized", and Application Support/GreatDANE. Anything else under /Volumes needs
  --allow-volume DIR or DANE_SIGN_ALLOW_VOLUMES.
- L2: the signing identity is never printed (the log shows "<identity redacted; team ...>", and it's
  scrubbed from codesign stderr).
- L3: the team ID comes from greatdane/macos/signing.conf (TEAM_ID). sign-map.tsv and the
  dane.browser.xml header refer to it. A malformed config is refused, and a mismatch fails check.
- L7: --json without a value is refused cleanly (it used to raise IndexError).
- check reports why each row failed (entitlements / runtime / team / timestamp).
- greatdane/tests/sign_dane_macos_selftest.py: 39 cases, Linux-runnable, mock codesign, no real signing.

Prepared only. Not built, signed, notarized or published.
